# Catalog templates

Cargo Upwell starts with built-in templates, then overlays one user catalog by stable ID. A template entry requires `id`, `description`, and exactly one source: `path` or `git`.

## Select the catalog

Precedence from highest to lowest is:

1. the explicit path supplied by the caller, including CLI `--catalog`;
2. `UPWELL_CATALOG_PATH`;
3. the platform default from <Symbol path="cargo_upwell::init::catalog::default_catalog_path" />;
4. built-ins alone when no default path exists or the implicit default file is absent.

An explicitly selected or environment-selected file must exist and validate. The platform defaults are `~/Library/Application Support/org.upwell-rs.Upwell/catalog.toml` on macOS, `${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/upwell/catalog.toml` on Linux, and `%APPDATA%\upwell-rs\Upwell\config\catalog.toml` on Windows. Use `cargo upwell templates` to inspect the effective result and pass `--catalog` in automation rather than relying on a user's machine path.

## Define a local template

<Example title="Register a repository-local template">

```toml
schema = "1"

[[entries]]
type = "template"
id = "acme/service"
description = "Acme HTTP service with deployment defaults"
path = "templates/service"
```

Relative paths resolve from the catalog file's directory, not the process working directory. Absolute paths remain absolute.

</Example>

For a one-off template outside a catalog, `cargo upwell init --template-path ../template` selects it directly. That mode conflicts with `--template` and `--catalog`; it is an explicit override, not another catalog layer.

## Define a pinned Git template

```toml
[[entries]]
type = "template"
id = "acme/protocol"
description = "Acme protocol crate and macro workspace"
git = "https://github.com/acme/upwell-template-protocol.git"
revision = "4f7d7f6c7d6c2f96b66b8d7f9cbf28fd7282ea6e"
```

Git sources accept at most one of `branch`, `tag`, or `revision` (`rev` is accepted as an alias for `revision`). A repository without a reference follows upstream default-branch movement. A branch is convenient but mutable. Use a tag only when your release process protects it; use an exact revision for reproducible generation.

## Understand merging and collisions

The catalog validates namespaced lowercase IDs. A user template can replace a built-in template with the same ID; this is how an organization deliberately overrides `upwell/application`. Duplicate IDs within the user document are rejected.

Tools and renderers cannot reuse an effective template ID. A template must not specify both `path` and `git`, neither source, a Git selector with a local path, or multiple Git selectors. Empty source/reference values are rejected. TOML unknown fields are rejected by the schema.

<Callout type="warning" title="Description is required">

Every template entry must include a human-readable `description`. It is not inferred from the repository and omitting it is a catalog parse failure.

</Callout>

## Generate reproducibly

```sh
cargo upwell templates --catalog .upwell/catalog.toml

cargo upwell init apps/payments \
  --catalog .upwell/catalog.toml \
  --template acme/service \
  --name payments \
  --no-vcs
```

Pin the catalog and Git revision in source control, pass the template ID explicitly, and record `--define` inputs in automation. If workspace registration fails, the generator rolls back the generated directory, but external template hooks and network effects are outside that filesystem rollback.

The canonical schema implementation is available in <SrcRef path="crates/cargo-upwell/src/init/catalog.rs">the committed catalog source</SrcRef>.

## Troubleshoot templates

- `UnknownTemplate` includes effective IDs; run `templates` against the same catalog selector.
- `InvalidTemplateSource` means the entry did not specify exactly one source or mixed local/Git fields.
- `ConflictingGitReferences` means more than one branch/tag/revision was set.
- A relative path resolves unexpectedly when the catalog file moved; paths are catalog-relative.
- Generation changes between runs when a Git source is unpinned or a template consumes unrecorded inputs.

See <GuideRef slug="cargo-upwell/catalog/extensions">catalog extensions</GuideRef> and <GuideRef slug="cargo-upwell/cli/automation-and-completions">automation and completions</GuideRef>.
